HQBD v0.1.0 — NOTICE

This release combines two upstream benchmark sources. The HQBD packaging
(renamed IDs, unified index, mappings, runnability metadata) is provided with
the release; the upstream terms below continue to apply to the included
content.

================================================================================
CVDP v1.1.0
================================================================================

Source: CVDP (Comprehensive Verilog Design Problems) benchmark, version 1.1.0.
Included content: 872 cases copied from HQBD v0.0.1, which in turn derives from
CVDP v1.1.0. The seven JSONL files are byte-for-byte copies with only the
filename version prefix changed.

Modifications: case IDs were renamed from cvdp_* to hqbd_* in HQBD v0.0.1.
Case content, prompts, contexts, harnesses, and metadata are unchanged. See the
release-level LICENSE file and the upstream CVDP distribution for the full
terms, including the no-commercial and commercial split conditions.

================================================================================
HWE-bench 0.1.0
================================================================================

Source project: https://github.com/pku-liang/hwe-bench
Paper: arXiv:2604.14709
Version: 0.1.0 (local snapshot dated 2026-09-09)
License: Apache License 2.0. A copy is included as LICENSE-HWE-bench.

Included content: all 417 bug-repair cases from the upstream
hwe_bench_full.jsonl, in native HWE format, merged and split by repository.

Modifications:
- the numeric GitHub pull-request id was renamed source_pr_id;
- the top-level id was replaced with hqbd_hwe_<repo_slug>_<pr-number>;
- hqbd_* provenance and runnability fields were appended;
- records were regrouped into per-repository files.
No native upstream field was removed or altered.

Upstream repositories represented in the HWE-bench portion:

  lowRISC/opentitan
  OpenXiangShan/XiangShan
  lowRISC/ibex
  openhwgroup/cva6
  chipsalliance/rocket-chip
  chipsalliance/caliptra-rtl

The HWE-bench dataset declares Apache-2.0 at the dataset level. The individual
licenses of these upstream repositories, and of the code included in their
patches and contexts, were not verified in this package. Each record carries a
base commit in base.sha; consult the upstream repository at that commit for the
applicable license. See licenses/upstream-repos.md. Do not assume that the
dataset-level license clears commercial use of the upstream code.

